    "domainName": "2. Advanced Math",
    "subtopicId": "nonlinear-functions",
    "subtopic": "Nonlinear functions & quadratics",
    "difficulty": "easy",
    "stem": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The <em>y</em>-intercept of the graph shown is <math alttext=\"left parenthesis x comma y right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>. What is the value of <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi></math>?</p>",
    "type": "grid-in",
    "correctAnswer": "40",
    "explanation": "<p>The correct answer is <math alttext=\"40\"><mn>40</mn></math>. The <em>y</em>-intercept of a graph in the <em>xy</em>-plane is the point <math alttext=\"left parenthesis x comma y right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> on the graph where <math alttext=\"x equals 0\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. The <em>y</em>-intercept of the graph shown is <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 0 comma 40 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>40</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. Therefore, the value of <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi></math> is <math alttext=\"40\"><mn>40</mn></math>.</p>",
