    "section": "math",
    "domainId": "advanced-math",
    "domainName": "2. Advanced Math",
    "subtopicId": "nonlinear-functions",
    "subtopic": "Nonlinear functions & quadratics",
    "difficulty": "easy",
    "stem": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The graph of the polynomial function <math alttext=\"f\"><mi>f</mi></math>, where <math alttext=\"y equals f left parenthesis x right parenthesis\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>, is shown. The <em>y</em>-intercept of the graph is <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 0 comma y right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>. What is the value of <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi></math>?</p>",
    "type": "grid-in",
    "correctAnswer": "4",
    "explanation": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The correct answer is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn></math>. The <em>y</em>-intercept of the graph of a function in the <em>xy</em>-plane is the point where the graph intersects the <em>y</em>-axis. The graph of the polynomial function shown intersects the <em>y</em>-axis at the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis 0 comma 4 right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo></math>. It's given that the <em>y</em>-intercept of the graph is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis 0 comma y right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>)</mo></math>. Therefore, the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn></math>.</p>",
