    "stem": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">What is the <em>x</em>-intercept of the graph shown?</p>",
    "type": "mcq",
    "correctAnswer": "B",
    "explanation": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is correct. An <em>x</em>-intercept of a graph in the <em>xy</em>-plane is a point at which the graph crosses the <em>x</em>-axis. The graph shown crosses the <em>x</em>-axis at the point <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 5 comma 0 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. Therefore, the <em>x</em>-intercept of the graph shown is <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 5 comma 0 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>",
