    "difficulty": "medium",
    "stem": "<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals x Superscript 5 Baseline plus 9 x plus 17\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>9</mn></mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>17</mn></mrow></math></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">For the given function <math alttext=\"f\"><mi>f</mi></math>, the graph of <math alttext=\"y equals f left parenthesis x right parenthesis\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> in the <em>xy</em>-plane passes through the point <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 0 comma b right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, where <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi></math> is a constant. What is the value of <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi></math>?</p>",
    "type": "grid-in",
    "correctAnswer": "17",
    "explanation": "<p>The correct answer is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"17\"><mn>17</mn></math>. It's given that the graph of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y equals f left parenthesis x right parenthesis\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math> in the <em>xy</em>-plane passes through the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis 0 comma b right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>)</mo></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi></math> is a constant. It follows that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f left parenthesis 0 right parenthesis\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></math> equals <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi></math>. Substituting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"0\"><mn>0</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi></math> in the given function yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f left parenthesis 0 right parenthesis equals 0 Superscript 5 Baseline plus 9 left parenthesis 0 right parenthesis plus 17\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>0</mn><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>17</mn></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f left parenthesis 0 right parenthesis equals 17\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>17</mn></math>. Therefore, the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"17\"><mn>17</mn></math>.</p>"
