    "subtopicId": "nonlinear-functions",
    "subtopic": "Nonlinear functions & quadratics",
    "difficulty": "hard",
    "stem": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">According to a model, the estimated volume of a certain tree in a forest increases by <math alttext=\"13.9 percent sign\"><mn>13.9</mn><mo>%</mo></math> for every increase of <math alttext=\"100\"><mn>100</mn></math> centimeters in the tree's height. The equation <math alttext=\"y equals a b Superscript StartFraction x Over 100 EndFraction\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>b</mi><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>100</mn></mfrac></msup></math> represents this model, where <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi></math> represents the estimated volume, in cubic centimeters, of this tree in the forest, <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi></math> represents the tree's height, in centimeters, and <math alttext=\"a\"><mi>a</mi></math> and <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi></math> are constants. In this equation, what is the value of <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi></math>?</p>",
    "type": "mcq",
    "correctAnswer": "C",
    "explanation": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is correct. It's given that equation <math alttext=\"y equals a b Superscript StartFraction x Over 100 EndFraction\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>b</mi><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>100</mn></mfrac></msup></math> represents the model, where <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi></math> is the estimated volume, in cubic centimeters, of a certain tree in a forest and <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi></math> is the tree's height, in centimeters. For an exponential equation of this form to represent a model where the value of <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi></math> increases as the value of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi></math> increases, it must follow that the values of <math alttext=\"a\"><mi>a</mi></math> and <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi></math> are positive. It's also given that the tree's estimated volume increases by <math alttext=\"13.9 percent sign\"><mn>13.9</mn>\n<mo>%</mo></math> for every increase of <math alttext=\"100\"><mn>100</mn></math> centimeters in the tree's height. Therefore, for every <math alttext=\"100\"><mn>100</mn></math>-centimeter increase in the tree's height, the estimated volume of the tree is <math alttext=\"1.139\"><mn>1.139</mn></math> times larger. In other words, <math alttext=\"a b Superscript StartFraction x plus 100 Over 100 EndFraction Baseline equals 1.139 a b Superscript StartFraction x Over 100 EndFraction\"><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>b</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><mn>100</mn></mfrac></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1.139</mn><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>b</mi><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>100</mn></mfrac></msup></math>, which is equivalent to <math alttext=\"a b Superscript StartFraction x Over 100 EndFraction Baseline b Superscript StartFraction 100 Over 100 EndFraction Baseline equals 1.139 a b Superscript StartFraction x Over 100 EndFraction\"><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>b</mi><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>100</mn></mfrac></msup><msup><mi>b</mi><mfrac><mn>100</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1.139</mn><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>b</mi><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>100</mn></mfrac></msup></math>. Since <math alttext=\"a\"><mi>a</mi></math> and <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi></math> are positive, dividing both sides of this equation by <math alttext=\"a b Superscript StartFraction x Over 100 EndFraction\"><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>b</mi><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>100</mn></mfrac></msup></math> yields <math alttext=\"b Superscript StartFraction 100 Over 100 EndFraction Baseline equals 1.139\"><msup><mi>b</mi><mfrac><mn>100</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1.139</mn></math>, or <math alttext=\"b equals 1.139\"><mrow>\n<mi>b</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>1.139</mn>\n</mrow></math>. Therefore, the value of <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi></math> is <math alttext=\"1.139\"><mn>1.139</mn></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect. This is the given percent increase in decimal form, not the value of <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect. This is the given percent increase, not the value of <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi></math>.</p>",
